# HTTPS in front of Mnemosyne with a name in your own domain (docs/team-server.md).
# Browsers only let a page use the microphone and share a call's audio over HTTPS.
# Replace the name; Caddy gets and renews the certificate itself (the name must resolve to
# this server, or use a DNS-challenge plugin for a name that is only on the office network).
mnemosyne.example.com {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8008
	# Meetings are uploaded and streamed through here: no body size limit, long timeouts.
	request_body {
		max_size 4GB
	}
}
